              </svg>
            </div>
            <p class="schematic-caption">
              <strong>Figure 2.3:</strong> DarkRISCV's microarchitecture routes instruction addresses through an asynchronous distributed LUT-RAM without clock latency. Register read ports (<code>U1REG</code>, <code>U2REG</code>) are pure combinational wires into the ALU. When a branch or jump is evaluated in the ALU (<code>BMUX</code>), the internal <strong>Branch Logic (driven by the ALU comparator &bull; completely independent of the DarkBridge data bus)</strong> redirects the program counter (<code>JVAL = PC + SIMM</code>) back to <code>IFPC</code> and simultaneously asserts a <code>FLUSH</code> pulse into the Decoder to squash the prefetched instruction (1-cycle penalty). DarkBridge operates strictly as an independent off-chip data memory/IO interface for loads and stores.
            </p>
