        <!-- 2.3.2 VEXRISCV DEEP-DIVE -->
        <div class="sub-topic-card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
          <div class="sub-topic-head">
            <div class="sub-topic-title-group">
              <span class="pill-badge badge-lime">CORE 7</span>
              <h4 class="sub-topic-title">VexRiscv &bull; 5-Stage Classic RISC</h4>
            </div>
            <span class="sub-topic-spec-badge">~42.0 kGE</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            Generated via <strong>SpinalHDL</strong> by Charles Papon, <strong>VexRiscv</strong> won the FSiC 2018 Soft CPU contest. In its <em>GenFull</em> configuration, it implements the textbook 5-stage RISC pipeline complete with dynamic branch prediction and full hazard resolution:
          </p>
          <ul class="concept-list">
            <li><strong>Classical 5-Stage Pipeline (IF &rarr; ID &rarr; EX &rarr; MEM &rarr; WB):</strong> The classic Hennessy &amp; Patterson five-stage pipeline maximizes temporal instruction parallelism. Every phase of instruction life has dedicated cycle resources.</li>
            <li><strong>Three-Level Forwarding Matrix:</strong> Features bypass networks routing results directly from <code>EX &rarr; EX</code>, <code>MEM &rarr; EX</code>, and <code>WB &rarr; EX</code>. Back-to-back mathematical operations execute with zero bubble stalls (instantaneous CPI = 1.0).</li>
            <li><strong>Load-Use Interlock Detection:</strong> When an instruction in the Decode stage requires a value loaded by a preceding <code>lw</code> instruction in Execute, the hardware hazard detection unit automatically stalls IF/ID by exactly 1 clock cycle to allow the memory word to return.</li>
            <li><strong>Dynamic BTB Branch Predictor:</strong> Features a Branch Target Buffer (BTB) that predicts branch outcomes during the IF stage. Correctly predicted branches incur <strong>zero bubble cycles</strong>, maintaining pipeline saturation through tight loops.</li>
            <li><strong>Dedicated Pipelined DSP Multiplier:</strong> Leverages FPGA DSP48E1 slices or ASIC standard-cell Booth multipliers to execute 32&times;32 multiplications in a single cycle.</li>
          </ul>

